// APNT shielded pool v1: the root-copy covenant (task 3.3).
//
// Target: protocol-design, "Note tree,
// root copies and the tree update"; specs/apnt-pool-note-tree/spec.md, "Roots
// are carried by interchangeable root copies".
//
// Maturity: new. Deterministic local-VM evidence only
// (packages/reference-aggregator/test/apnt_pool_tree_covenants_v1_local_vm.test.ts).
// Not deployed, not frozen, not a chain claim.
//
// A root copy is a keyless UTXO under this lock holding an immutable NFT of
// the root category T whose 32-byte commitment is a folded root. A copy is
// spent only by a settlement, which recreates it:
//
//   authority   input 0 carries a verdict-category token with no capability
//               and is under the pool settlement lock (the settlement
//               authority of apnt-pool-settlement-custody);
//   recreation  the hinted output o is under this same lock and carries this
//               input's token category (with its capability byte) and
//               commitment, and at least this input's value;
//   rank        the inputs before this one under this lock number exactly as
//               many as the outputs before o under this lock. Distinct copy
//               inputs therefore map to distinct outputs, so two copies of
//               one root cannot be recreated as one.
//
// The covenant compares the output with this input's own token rather than
// with a pinned category: whatever sits under this lock is recreated
// unchanged. Only T's immutable NFTs are copies; the settlement covenant
// (task 3.4, check 3) must require the root category with no capability, and
// cannot identify copies by this lock, because this lock embeds the
// settlement lock.
//
// Unlocking data (before the P2SH32 redeem push): <o>.
//
// Cost: the rank loops read every input before this one and every output
// before o, so a copy placed early in the settlement is cheaper.
//
// `//@check NAME` … `//@end` mark one covenant check; the local-VM tests remove
// one at a time.
//
// Local VM acceptance is not chain validation, proof verification, wallet
// acceptance or spendability.

// Stack on entry: o.

// Settlement authority: input 0 holds a verdict-category token with no
// capability ...
//@check AUTH_CATEGORY
<0> OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY @VERDICT_CATEGORY_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
// ... under the pool settlement lock.
//@check AUTH_LOCK
<0> OP_UTXOBYTECODE @SETTLEMENT_LOCK_PUSH@ OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end

// Output o recreates this copy.
//@check OUT_LOCK
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOBYTECODE OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check OUT_CATEGORY
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCATEGORY OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOTOKENCATEGORY OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check OUT_COMMITMENT
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOTOKENCOMMITMENT OP_EQUALVERIFY
//@end
//@check OUT_VALUE
OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTVALUE OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOVALUE OP_GREATERTHANOREQUAL OP_VERIFY
//@end

//@check RANK
OP_INPUTINDEX OP_UTXOBYTECODE <0> <0>
// Stack: o L count idx, with L this input's locking bytecode.
OP_INPUTINDEX OP_OVER OP_GREATERTHAN
OP_IF
  OP_BEGIN
    OP_DUP OP_UTXOBYTECODE <3> OP_PICK OP_EQUAL
    OP_ROT OP_ADD OP_SWAP OP_1ADD
    OP_DUP OP_INPUTINDEX OP_NUMEQUAL
  OP_UNTIL
OP_ENDIF
OP_DROP
<0> <0>
// Stack: o L rank_in count idx.
<4> OP_PICK OP_OVER OP_GREATERTHAN
OP_IF
  OP_BEGIN
    OP_DUP OP_OUTPUTBYTECODE <4> OP_PICK OP_EQUAL
    OP_ROT OP_ADD OP_SWAP OP_1ADD
    OP_DUP <5> OP_PICK OP_NUMEQUAL
  OP_UNTIL
OP_ENDIF
OP_DROP
// Stack: o L rank_in rank_out.
OP_NUMEQUALVERIFY OP_DROP
//@end

OP_DROP <1>
